{"text": "Once a king thought that he would never fail in anything if he knew three things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He wanted to know the right time to begin every task and the right people to listen to. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Above all, he wanted to know which work was the most important of all. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> So he sent a message throughout his kingdom, promising a great reward to anyone who could teach him these things. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Many learned men came to the king, but they all gave different answers. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Some said that he should make a careful timetable of days, months, and years and follow it strictly. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Others said that he should always pay attention to what was happening and do what was most needed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Still others said that he needed a council of wise men, and some even said he should ask magicians. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To the second question, some answered that his advisers were the most important, while others named priests, doctors, or soldiers. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To the third question, some said science, some said skill in war, and others said the worship of God. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The answers were so different that the king agreed with none of them and gave nobody the reward.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "n", "c", "e", " ", "a", " ", "k", "i", "n", "g", " ", "t", "h", "o", "u", "g", "h", "t", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "h", "e", " ", "w", "o", "u", "l", "d", " ", "n", "e", "v", "e", "r", " ", "f", "a", "i", "l", " ", "i", "n", " ", "a", "n", "y", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "i", "f", " ", "h", "e", " ", "k", "n", "e", "w", " ", "t", "h", "r", "e", "e", " ", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "H", "e", " ", "w", "a", "n", "t", "e", "d", " ", "t", "o", " ", "k", "n", "o", "w", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "r", "i", "g", "h", "t", " ", 